  "limitations": [
    "Candidate source is the public 1.1.0 release plus the telemetry consent fix, security dependency updates, npm bundled postcss-selector-parser patch, a narrow expiring ignore for the unreachable Temporal core-bridge rustls advisory and the restored small-profile readiness gate; it was not re-exported from the private production source.",
    "VM hosts are x86_64. ARM64 container validation remains a release workflow gate.",
    "Fresh installer timings use preloaded local candidate images; they exclude network image downloads.",
    "Large profiles ran with temporary 16 GiB/8 CPU lab resources (and Docker Desktop 8 GiB/8 CPU on macOS/Windows); every runner was restored to 8 GiB/4 CPU afterwards.",
    "macOS: in the previous candidate run a devtest file written about 30 s before the guest restart was lost (Docker Desktop did not flush it); reboot proofs now run after a filesystem sync on every platform.",
    "Windows desktop commands ran as interactive scheduled tasks in an owned RDP session; this is not keystroke coverage of every wizard prompt.",
    "First AI task: on Linux two attempts and on macOS one attempt stalled because the OpenCode Zen free model ling-3.1-flash-free returned repeated upstream request failures (recorded in evidence/*-first-agent-attempt*-stalled.json); each retry used a new pane in the same owned proof room and a new prompt marker, and the accepted proof is the completed native session.",
    "The free model is chosen by the first-run check, which verifies a plain completion only; a model that passes it can still fail upstream on tool-call follow-ups. Tracked as a product follow-up.",
    "npm next publication, environment approval and latest promotion have not yet completed."
